<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed steady on Sunday but are expected to rise after an increase in the domestic prices of raw cotton, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchants Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Sunday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    510	    510</p>
<p>    Globe (Hina)		 505	    505</p>
<p>    M.G.M.			 500	    500</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
